<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kunduz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kunduz is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, capital of Kunduz province, on the Kunduz River in the fertile plain of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>. It was a capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokharistan">Tokharistan</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> and the Turkic yabghus, and in the 19th century the seat of Murad Beg's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> khanate of Kataghan. It remains a key junction on the road to Tajikistan.</p></div>
